  "details": "I have two moderation and safety features that I think could help group instances.\n\n1. Group-Based Instance Restrictions\n\nGroup owners should have the option to block members of certain groups from joining their group instances.\n\nFor example, imagine I run a group instance and there is another group whose members have repeatedly caused problems in our community. Instead of moderators having to deal with those users individually every time, the group owner could add that group to an instance block list.\n\nIf a player is currently a member of a blocked group, that player would be prevented from joining the instance.\n\nHowever, if the player is also a member of the group hosting the instance, the hosting group's membership could take priority so legitimate members are not accidentally denied access.\n\nThis would give group owners another preventative moderation tool rather than requiring moderators to wait for problems to occur before taking action.\n\n2. Instance-Wide Avatar Hiding\n\nI would also like an additional moderation option for group instance moderators that temporarily hides a specific avatar for everyone in that instance.\n\nFor example, when a moderator opens a player's menu, there could be another moderation option near controls such as Warn, Kick, Force Mute, and Ban called something like:\n\nHide Avatar for Instance\n\nWhen selected, the player's avatar would be hidden for everyone currently in that instance.\n\nThis could be useful when somebody joins using an avatar that is causing performance problems or other disruption. Instead of every player having to manually hide the avatar, an authorized instance moderator could temporarily hide it for everyone.\n\nThe restriction could automatically reset when the instance closes. Alternatively, there could be a second option allowing the moderator to restore the avatar manually.\n\nThe important distinction is that this would not globally ban the avatar from VRChat. It would only hide that avatar for people inside that particular group instance.\n\nThese features would give group moderators additional tools to proactively protect their instances while keeping the effects limited to the communities and instances they moderate.",
